# CODEOWNERS — who must review changes to each path before merge.
# Step 1.2c of docs/runbook.md: replace the team handles below with your real GitHub teams,
# then ask the repo admin to enable on `main`:
#   Branch protection -> "Require a pull request before merging" -> "Require review from Code Owners"
#   Branch protection -> "Require signed commits"
# Together with the Builder's git-log check (agents/builder-agent.md Step 00), this is what makes
# an approval.json an audit-grade approval rather than a text file.

# Approvals: only BAs and engineering leads may add or change an approval record.
runs/**/approval.json        @your-org/ba-team @your-org/engineering-leads

# The map itself: service owners + engineering leads.
manifests/                   @your-org/engineering-leads
schema/                      @your-org/engineering-leads
config/                      @your-org/engineering-leads

# Agent behaviour: engineering leads only (generated adapters follow the canonical files).
agents/                      @your-org/engineering-leads
.github/agents/              @your-org/engineering-leads
.claude/agents/              @your-org/engineering-leads
AGENTS.md                    @your-org/engineering-leads
templates/                   @your-org/engineering-leads
prompts/                     @your-org/engineering-leads
